<title>USA: BEFORE THE BELL - Great Western up on new bid.</title>
<headline>BEFORE THE BELL - Great Western up on new bid.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Great Western Financial Corp shares climbed to 47-1/4 from 45 before Thursday's market open in buying driven by Washington Mutual Savings Bank's friendly bid for the company to rival a hostile, less lucrative takeover attempt by H.F. Ahmanson and Co.</p>
<p>At the same time, Washington Mutual shed 1/4 to to 53.</p>
<p>Early this morning, Washington and Great Western said they agreed to a stock-swap merger with a ratio of 0.9 Washington shares for each Great Western share.</p>
<p>Including this morning's stock moves, the terms value Great Western at $47.70 per share.</p>
</text>
